## Problem Statement

### The Context Amnesia Problem

AI coding tools create a critical workflow problem:

| Issue | Impact | Example |
|-------|--------|---------|
| **Lost Context** | Every session starts fresh | Re-explaining requirements to AI |
| **Unfinished Work** | Requirements get forgotten | "Add tests" mentioned but never tracked |
| **Repeated Mistakes** | No record of failures | Trying abandoned approaches again |
| **No Traceability** | Can't see decision rationale | Why was this architecture chosen? |

### Target Users

**AI-Native Developers** who:
- Use AI coding agents daily (Cursor, Codex, Copilot)
- Work on complex features spanning multiple sessions
- Need to resume work after breaks or team handoffs
- Want to understand the "why" behind code changes

### Why This Matters

- **Productivity Loss**: 30% time wasted re-explaining context (estimated)
- **Quality Degradation**: Important requirements lost between sessions
- **Knowledge Silos**: Team members can't pick up each other's AI sessions
- **No Institutional Memory**: Design decisions lost after project completion

